Most of those systems were themselves normalised by Open Design from bergside/awesome-design-skills
(https://github.com/bergside/awesome-design-skills, commit f631a09b4fcc0166f2e2c1a8c81906ef680c57e8),
Copyright (c) 2026 Bergside, License: MIT (see LICENSE.bergside in this folder).

Changes made for Swarm Studio (scripts/import-od-systems.mjs; decision 0016):
- packs.json keeps the colours (surface, text, primary, secondary), the heading and body font, the
  medium corner radius (in px) and the first line of the visual theme.
- systems.json keeps, per system: the tokens of the first :root block in tokens.css without its comments,
  colours and fonts (the brand sheet's palette and type are the colours and fonts) and without the names
  Swarm's pages already define; a digest of DESIGN.md (the first line of the visual theme, the first four
  do's and don'ts or anti-patterns, shortened); and the labels of the component groups in
  components.manifest.json. Dropped: the rest of DESIGN.md, components.html, previews and Tailwind files.
- Fonts that are not Google Fonts families, and display faces used as body text, are replaced; each
  replacement is listed in the pack's `dropped` field.
- Who each look is for, the words that suggest it, the voice, the picture style and the storyboard
  were written for Swarm Studio; they are not from either source.
- Every system is imported, the ones named after a real company or product too (decision 0016); they
  are Open Design's aesthetic inspirations, not official assets of those companies.

